[ti:How New Hardware Finds Its Way into PyTorch]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: You’ve built a new accelerator. It runs your model.
[00:00.00]Ava：你造了一款新加速器，模型也跑起来了。
[00:03.76]Then PyTorch changes, and you’re back fixing patches. How do we make that less painful?
[00:03.76]可 PyTorch 一更新，你又得修补丁。怎么才能省点力？
[00:10.53]Brian: That’s the problem behind this article.
[00:10.53]Brian：这正是这篇文章要解决的问题。
[00:13.14]The Accelerator Integration Working Group wants clearer integration paths, shared tests, and earlier feedback when upstream changes break something.
[00:13.14]加速器集成工作组希望明确集成路径、共用测试，并在上游改动造成问题时更早收到反馈。
[00:23.40]Ava: I’m Ava.
[00:23.40]Ava：我是 Ava。
[00:24.00]I’m a software engineer outside the PyTorch core team, and maintaining a pile of patches sounds painfully familiar.
[00:24.00]我不是 PyTorch 核心团队的工程师，但维护一堆补丁的痛苦，我太熟悉了。
[00:32.87]Brian: And I’m Brian.
[00:32.87]Brian：我是 Brian。
[00:33.85]Today we’re looking at the group’s progress in the first half of twenty twenty-six, from testing to compiler support.
[00:33.85]今天我们来看看工作组在 2026 年上半年的进展，从测试到编译器支持。
[00:42.34]Ava: Let’s start with the motivation. Why does hardware integration need a working group?
[00:42.34]Ava：先说说初衷。为什么硬件集成需要一个工作组？
[00:48.65]Brian: More compute platforms are adopting PyTorch.
[00:48.65]Brian：越来越多的计算平台开始采用 PyTorch。
[00:51.85]Each backend, meaning the implementation connecting hardware to the framework, needs reliable ways to fit into the same system.
[00:51.85]每个后端，也就是连接硬件与框架的实现，都需要可靠的方式接入同一套系统。
[01:01.45]Ava: Like different appliances needing a standard socket, instead of everyone opening the wall and rewiring it?
[01:01.45]Ava：就像不同电器都该用标准插座，不用每家都拆墙改线？
[01:09.12]Brian: Exactly.
[01:09.12]Brian：没错。
[01:09.72]The group works on vendor-neutral mechanisms, shared tools, and reference implementations.
[01:09.72]工作组致力于建立不依赖特定厂商的机制、共用工具和参考实现。
[01:16.39]Those help hardware teams avoid maintaining their own framework patches.
[01:16.39]这样硬件团队就不用各自维护框架补丁了。
[01:22.07]Ava: Where does the feedback problem come in?
[01:22.07]Ava：反馈问题又是怎么回事？
[01:24.85]Brian: PyTorch’s upstream repository, where framework development happens, has extensive continuous integration, or CI.
[01:24.85]Brian：PyTorch 的上游代码库是框架开发的地方，那里有完善的持续集成，也就是 CI。
[01:33.37]That’s automated testing of changes. But dependent projects run tests elsewhere.
[01:33.37]CI 会自动测试代码改动，但依赖 PyTorch 的项目在别处运行测试。
[01:39.81]Ava: Those are the downstream projects.
[01:39.81]Ava：这些就是下游项目。
[01:42.24]Hardware backends and libraries that depend on PyTorch?
[01:42.24]比如依赖 PyTorch 的硬件后端和库？
[01:46.52]Brian: Right. They lacked a standard way to receive change notifications and return results.
[01:46.52]Brian：对。之前没有标准方式向它们发送变更通知并收回测试结果。
[01:52.42]Contributors couldn’t easily see downstream damage before merging a change.
[01:52.42]贡献者很难在合并改动前发现对下游的影响。
[01:57.98]Ava: So the warning could arrive after the change was already in?
[01:57.98]Ava：所以等收到警报，改动可能已经合并了？
[02:01.93]Brian: Yes. Cross-Repository CI Relay, or CRCR, connects those separate testing systems.
[02:01.93]Brian：是的。跨仓库 CI 中继系统（Cross-Repository CI Relay，简称 CRCR）把这些独立的测试系统连接起来。
[02:08.56]A pull request, meaning a proposed code change, or a pushed commit triggers notifications.
[02:08.56]拉取请求，也就是提议的代码改动，或推送的提交，都会触发通知。
[02:16.28]Ava: And every registered project gets its own chance to test?
[02:16.28]Ava：每个已注册的项目都能自己测试？
[02:20.68]Brian: They’re notified in parallel.
[02:20.68]Brian：它们会同时收到通知。
[02:23.03]Each repository runs its own workflow, then sends its status back.
[02:23.03]每个代码库运行自己的工作流，再把状态报回来。
[02:28.37]Results appear in PyTorch’s shared CI dashboard within seconds.
[02:28.37]结果上报后，几秒内就会出现在 PyTorch 的共享 CI 看板上。
[02:33.82]Ava: Within seconds of reporting, though.
[02:33.82]Ava：是上报后几秒内。
[02:36.57]That doesn’t mean a huge test suite finishes in seconds.
[02:36.57]这可不是说庞大的测试套件几秒就能跑完。
[02:41.18]Brian: Right. The article describes fast result delivery.
[02:41.18]Brian：对。文章说的是结果传递得快。
[02:44.88]It doesn’t promise that the tests themselves run that quickly.
[02:44.88]并没说测试本身也能跑得那么快。
[02:49.81]Ava: How does PyTorch know who’s reporting?
[02:49.81]Ava：PyTorch 怎么知道是谁在上报？
[02:52.53]A green check needs a little more evidence than, trust me.
[02:52.53]要给绿色通过标记，总不能只凭一句“相信我”吧。
[02:57.03]Brian: GitHub OpenID Connect, or OIDC, tokens verify the calling repository’s identity.
[02:57.03]Brian：GitHub OpenID Connect（OIDC）令牌会验证调用方代码库的身份。
[03:03.53]There are also authorization checks, rate limits, and checks on valid reporting state.
[03:03.53]此外还有权限检查、速率限制，以及对上报状态是否有效的检查。
[03:10.86]Ava: Does joining immediately give a downstream project power to block changes?
[03:10.86]Ava：下游项目一加入，就能阻止改动合并吗？
[03:16.23]Brian: No.
[03:16.23]Brian：不能。
[03:16.44]Four participation levels move from notifications through dashboard reporting to non-blocking and eventually blocking checks.
[03:16.44]参与分为四级：从接收通知、在看板展示结果，到不阻止合并的检查，最后才是能阻止合并的检查。
[03:25.00]Trusted information stays separate from self-reported data.
[03:25.00]可信信息与项目自行上报的数据也会分开。
[03:29.40]Ava: Got it. Shared visibility, with controlled participation.
[03:29.40]Ava：明白了。大家都能看到结果，参与权限也受到控制。
[03:34.06]But teams still need useful tests to run.
[03:34.06]但团队还得有用得上的测试。
[03:37.76]Brian: Exactly. PyTorch has over six hundred thousand test cases.
[03:37.76]Brian：没错。PyTorch 有超过 60 万个测试用例。
[03:42.21]Many were tied to particular hardware through fixed device names or backend-specific operations.
[03:42.21]其中很多通过写死的设备名称或特定后端操作，绑定到了某类硬件。
[03:49.92]Ava: So a test might check a general feature, but its setup only lets one accelerator through the door?
[03:49.92]Ava：也就是说，测试检查的可能是通用功能，但测试配置只允许一种加速器运行？
[03:56.49]Brian: That’s the issue. Other vendors had to patch tests.
[03:56.49]Brian：问题就在这儿。其他厂商只好给测试打补丁。
[04:00.18]The refactoring replaces fixed hardware references with device parameters, so the same logic can serve multiple backends.
[04:00.18]这次重构用设备参数替代写死的硬件引用，让同一套测试逻辑适用于多个后端。
[04:09.29]Ava: How much progress did they report?
[04:09.29]Ava：他们报告了多少进展？
[04:11.87]Brian: Contributors migrated over two hundred seventy-six test files in the first half of the year.
[04:11.87]Brian：今年上半年，贡献者迁移了超过 276 个测试文件。
[04:18.16]They covered areas including profiling, neural network modules, and optimizers.
[04:18.16]他们涉及的领域包括性能分析、神经网络模块和优化器。
[04:23.91]Ava: But some tests really are hardware-specific. You can’t make every test universal.
[04:23.91]Ava：但有些测试确实依赖特定硬件，不可能让所有测试都通用。
[04:30.45]Brian: Right.
[04:30.45]Brian：对。
[04:30.96]Classes fall into three groups: accelerator-unrelated, accelerator-agnostic, and accelerator-specific.
[04:30.96]测试类分为三类：与加速器无关、适用于不同加速器，以及特定加速器专用。
[04:39.60]In plain English, that’s no accelerator needed, reusable across devices, or tied to one backend.
[04:39.60]简单说，就是不需要加速器、可跨设备复用，或绑定某个后端。
[04:48.08]Ava: And that classification helps select the right tests?
[04:48.08]Ava：这样分类有助于选对测试？
[04:52.42]Brian: Yes. The metadata and selection flag work across the test execution paths.
[04:52.42]Brian：是的。元数据和选择标志适用于各条测试执行路径。
[04:58.06]A linter, an automated rule checker, requires new test classes to declare their classification.
[04:58.06]代码检查工具会要求新的测试类声明所属类别。
[05:05.66]Ava: What happens to all the old ones?
[05:05.66]Ava：那已有的测试类怎么办？
[05:08.74]Brian: They’re being handled gradually.
[05:08.74]Brian：正在逐步处理。
[05:11.13]At launch, one thousand one hundred ninety-one unclassified files were on an allowlist.
[05:11.13]推出时，允许名单上有 1191 个尚未分类的文件。
[05:17.61]Reducing that list is ongoing work.
[05:17.61]缩减这份名单仍在进行。
[05:20.56]Ava: What if my backend only supports some features?
[05:20.56]Ava：如果我的后端只支持部分功能呢？
[05:24.08]Brian: There’s fine-grained skipping by feature, class, test, and operator.
[05:24.08]Brian：可以按功能、类、测试和算子精细地跳过测试。
[05:28.79]Vendors can select what matches their implementation without changing upstream test code.
[05:28.79]厂商无需修改上游测试代码，就能选择符合自身实现的测试。
[05:35.30]Ava: So we’ve got reusable tests and clearer selection.
[05:35.30]Ava：这样测试能复用，选择方式也更清晰了。
[05:38.87]Now, where do developers learn the actual integration patterns?
[05:38.87]那么，开发者去哪里学习具体的集成方式？
[05:43.72]Brian: That’s OpenReg’s role.
[05:43.72]Brian：这正是 OpenReg 的作用。
[05:45.33]It’s a minimal reference backend built on PrivateUse1, PyTorch’s mechanism for integrating custom accelerator backends.
[05:45.33]它是基于 PrivateUse1 构建的最小参考后端；PrivateUse1 是 PyTorch 集成自定义加速器后端的机制。
[05:54.39]Ava: Does OpenReg need special hardware?
[05:54.39]Ava：OpenReg 需要专用硬件吗？
[05:57.59]Brian: No. It’s backed by the central processing unit, or CPU.
[05:57.59]Brian：不需要。它由中央处理器，也就是 CPU，提供支持。
[06:01.63]It lives inside PyTorch’s source tree and demonstrates integration mechanics without real accelerator complexity.
[06:01.63]它位于 PyTorch 源码树中，展示集成机制，无需涉及真实加速器的复杂性。
[06:10.28]Ava: Like a teaching engine with the important parts visible.
[06:10.28]Ava：就像一台能看清关键部件的教学用引擎。
[06:13.96]You wouldn’t enter it in a race.
[06:13.96]但不会拿它去参加比赛。
[06:16.41]Brian: Exactly. It isn’t a production backend.
[06:16.41]Brian：没错。它不是生产用后端。
[06:19.37]It demonstrates device registration, operator dispatch, meaning routing operations to implementations, and runtime behavior such as streams and events.
[06:19.37]它展示设备注册、算子分派，即将操作交给相应实现，以及流和事件等运行时行为。
[06:31.16]Ava: Streams organize device work, and events help track its progress?
[06:31.16]Ava：流负责组织设备上的工作，事件帮助跟踪进度？
[06:36.55]Brian: That’s the basic idea.
[06:36.55]Brian：基本就是这样。
[06:38.37]OpenReg also runs in CI, helping catch breaks in PrivateUse1 integration.
[06:38.37]OpenReg 也在持续集成（CI）中运行，帮助发现 PrivateUse1 集成中的问题。
[06:44.38]Its implementation is kept aligned with the integration documentation.
[06:44.38]它的实现会与集成文档保持一致。
[06:50.49]Ava: Let’s talk profiling. Knowing an operation took a long time isn’t always enough.
[06:50.49]Ava：说说性能分析。只知道某个操作耗时很长，有时还不够。
[06:57.05]Brian: Right.
[06:57.05]Brian：对。
[06:57.49]Developers also need timelines for kernels, the device computations, plus memory and runtime events.
[06:57.49]开发者还需要内核，也就是设备计算的时间线，以及内存和运行时事件的时间线。
[07:04.80]They need to connect host activity with device activity.
[07:04.80]他们需要把主机活动与设备活动对应起来。
[07:09.24]Ava: Like matching an order placed at the counter with the work happening in the kitchen?
[07:09.24]Ava：就像把柜台接到的订单和厨房里的工作对应起来？
[07:13.79]Brian: Yes. Correlation IDs provide that connection.
[07:13.79]Brian：对。关联 ID 就能建立这种联系。
[07:17.32]OpenReg’s reference profiling stack demonstrates those IDs, activity types, and the lifecycle of a profiling session.
[07:17.32]OpenReg 的参考性能分析组件展示了这些 ID、活动类型，以及一次性能分析会话的生命周期。
[07:26.86]Ava: Is it a complete profiler?
[07:26.86]Ava：它是完整的性能分析器吗？
[07:29.08]Brian: No. It’s a stub, a minimal implementation showing the connections.
[07:29.08]Brian：不是。它只是一个桩实现，用最少的代码展示各部分如何连接。
[07:34.25]It plugs into Kineto, the profiling system used here, through PyTorch’s registration interface.
[07:34.25]它通过 PyTorch 的注册接口接入这里使用的性能分析系统 Kineto。
[07:42.05]Ava: Then vendors replace the demonstration pieces with their own device profiling calls?
[07:42.05]Ava：然后厂商用自己的设备性能分析调用替换这些演示部分？
[07:47.97]Brian: Exactly, without modifying PyTorch or Kineto.
[07:47.97]Brian：正是如此，无需修改 PyTorch 或 Kineto。
[07:51.61]Tests cover registration, session lifecycle, and fallback behavior.
[07:51.61]测试覆盖注册、会话生命周期和回退行为。
[07:57.03]The older path remains available for coarse operator-level timing.
[07:57.03]旧路径仍可用于粗粒度的算子级计时。
[08:02.72]Ava: That’s a clearer starting point. Does the same approach extend to distributed training?
[08:02.72]Ava：这样入门就清楚多了。同样的方法也适用于分布式训练吗？
[08:08.88]Brian: Yes. The group began building OCCL, the OpenReg Collective Communications Library.
[08:08.88]Brian：是的。团队开始构建 OCCL，即 OpenReg 集合通信库。
[08:15.37]It’s a minimal reference for a custom backend in c10d, PyTorch’s distributed infrastructure.
[08:15.37]它是为 PyTorch 分布式基础设施 c10d 中的自定义后端提供的最小参考实现。
[08:23.00]Ava: What does it actually demonstrate?
[08:23.00]Ava：它具体展示了什么？
[08:25.80]Brian: Registering a ProcessGroup, which represents participating processes, dispatching collectives, meaning coordinated communication operations, and handling Work completion, meaning when an operation is considered finished.
[08:25.80]Brian：注册代表参与进程的 ProcessGroup、分派集合通信操作，以及处理 Work 的完成状态，也就是何时将操作视为完成。
[08:39.95]Ava: So again, the result is a clearer integration contract.
[08:39.95]Ava：所以，这同样让集成约定更清晰了。
[08:44.24]We’re not hearing a communication speed claim.
[08:44.24]我们听到的并不是通信速度方面的承诺。
[08:48.17]Brian: Correct. Production performance isn’t OCCL’s target.
[08:48.17]Brian：没错。OCCL 的目标不是生产环境的性能。
[08:52.06]Related work also improved support for Python-based distributed backends and device-generic distributed test selection.
[08:52.06]相关工作还改进了对基于 Python 的分布式后端，以及设备通用的分布式测试筛选的支持。
[09:01.29]Ava: How about compilation? That’s another big surface to connect.
[09:01.29]Ava：编译方面呢？这也是需要打通的重要环节。
[09:06.08]Brian: The OpenReg example shows integration with torch.
[09:06.08]Brian：OpenReg 示例展示了如何接入 torch。
[09:10.05]compile, PyTorch’s compilation entry point.
[09:10.05]compile，也就是 PyTorch 的编译入口。
[09:13.53]Dynamo handles graph capture and device management.
[09:13.53]Dynamo 负责图捕获和设备管理。
[09:17.66]Graph capture records operations for compilation.
[09:17.66]图捕获会记录操作，供编译使用。
[09:21.98]Ava: And where does Inductor fit?
[09:21.98]Ava：Inductor 在其中负责什么？
[09:24.42]Brian: Inductor offers scheduling, fusion, and code generation.
[09:24.42]Brian：Inductor 提供调度、融合和代码生成能力。
[09:28.85]Fusion combines operations into kernels.
[09:28.85]融合会把多个操作合并成内核。
[09:32.02]Vendors can optionally use those optimization passes, and OpenReg demonstrates the integration points.
[09:32.02]厂商可以选择使用这些优化流程；OpenReg 展示了相应的集成接口。
[09:40.44]Ava: Including fused kernel generation without changing upstream PyTorch?
[09:40.44]Ava：包括无须修改上游 PyTorch，就能生成融合内核？
[09:45.64]Brian: Yes. There’s also a compiler integration guide.
[09:45.64]Brian：对。另外还有一份编译器集成指南。
[09:49.22]Again, the focus is showing how the pieces connect, rather than reporting production performance.
[09:49.22]重点仍是展示各部分如何衔接，而不是报告生产环境的性能。
[09:56.96]Ava: What’s still ahead?
[09:56.96]Ava：接下来还有哪些工作？
[09:58.75]Brian: More test coverage, fewer unclassified tests, and connecting classification to automatic CI scheduling.
[09:58.75]Brian：扩大测试覆盖范围，减少未分类测试，并将分类结果用于 CI 自动调度。
[10:06.01]They’re also exploring a registry where accelerators declare supported operator data types and precision overrides.
[10:06.01]他们也在探索一个注册机制，让加速器声明支持的算子数据类型和精度覆盖设置。
[10:14.46]Ava: And once a platform’s integrated, how do users find it?
[10:14.46]Ava：平台集成后，用户怎么找到它？
[10:18.87]Brian: The official Additional Platforms page links from PyTorch’s install page.
[10:18.87]Brian：PyTorch 的安装页面链接到了官方的 Additional Platforms 页面。
[10:24.23]Admission requires evidence and review.
[10:24.23]平台要获收录，必须提供证明材料并通过审核。
[10:27.10]The group’s encouraging more vendors to apply in the second half.
[10:27.10]该小组鼓励更多厂商在下半年申请。
[10:32.22]Ava: Let’s recap three points.
[10:32.22]Ava：我们总结三点。
[10:34.39]First, CRCR brings downstream test feedback into a shared upstream view.
[10:34.39]第一，CRCR 将下游的测试反馈汇集到上游的共享视图中。
[10:40.97]Brian: Second, test refactoring helps backends reuse validation.
[10:40.97]Brian：第二，测试重构让后端能够复用验证流程。
[10:45.47]Third, OpenReg provides concrete integration references, while production readiness still requires further work.
[10:45.47]第三，OpenReg 提供了具体的集成参考，但要达到生产可用仍需进一步工作。
[10:54.64]Ava: Thanks for listening. We’ll see you next time.
[10:54.64]Ava：感谢收听，我们下期再见。
